2026-11-10T13:32Z reviewer created

--- body ---
## Context

Ticket 1516 (PR 2423, merged 2026-11-10) made `scripts/trace-compact-audit.py`
read the fleet by running the other host's own copy of the script over ssh.
The same day a default run on padme printed `Host doudou: COULD NOT LOOK`:
doudou's checkout predated the change and rejected the new flags. That will
recur after every change to the script until the other host syncs. The ssh
version also introduced a hardcoded host list, `FLEET_HOSTS = ("padme",
"doudou")`. Asked "Why not use the archive? Do we commit to run the audit
only on padme anyway?", and given the comparison, the author ruled on
2026-11-10: "Switch to archive".

Read on padme, 2026-11-10 (paths and counts only):

- The archive (`scripts/transcript_spool.py`, `scripts/agent-sessions-README.md`)
  is written nightly by `scripts/transcript_archive.py` (systemd user timer
  `transcript-archive`, 03:33); doudou pushes its `raw/doudou/` to padme over
  ssh. A source touched within the last day is skipped.
- padme's archive holds `raw/doudou/{claude,codex,pi,seat-raw}` and
  `launches.jsonl`: 28272 files, the newest dated 2026-11-08. One zstd file
  per source file, the original relative path kept:
  `raw/<host>/claude/<project>/<session>.jsonl.zst`,
  `raw/<host>/codex/YYYY/MM/DD/rollout-….jsonl.zst`,
  `raw/<host>/pi/<dir>/<file>.jsonl.zst`. `transcript_archive.py` reads a
  copy back with `zstd -dc`.
- doudou's own archive holds `raw/doudou` only. The fleet's transcripts sit
  together on padme alone.
- `spool/` on padme holds `spool/padme` only.

## Scope

- This host is read live, as today. Every other host is read from this
  host's archive, `raw/<host>/<runtime>`; the hosts are the directories the
  archive holds, no list in the script.
- Each host read from the archive is named with the date of its newest
  archived file, and the output says that a transcript touched within the
  last day is not in the archive yet.
- The ssh path goes: `FLEET_HOSTS`, the remote run, the flags that exist only
  for it, their tests and every statement of them (docstrings, help,
  `skills/trace-doctor/SKILL.md`). `--local` stays and reads this host alone.
- A host whose archive copy is absent or unreadable, an archive root that
  cannot be resolved, or an archive that holds no other host is reported as
  such, never as zero sessions: on a host that does not receive the others'
  archives the audit reads that host and says the fleet view is not available
  there.
- Archived transcripts are decompressed in memory or as a stream. No
  decompressed copy is written to disk, and the script opens no network
  connection.

Out of scope: reading this host's own archive copy (sessions deleted from the
live trees stay out, as today); changing the archive's schedule or its push;
`seat-raw` and `launches.jsonl`; any other trace script.

## Test

On a fixture archive built in a temporary directory, with a compressed
Claude Code, Codex and Pi transcript under `raw/<other>/`: a session past its
ceiling on the other host is counted under that host and runtime; the host's
line carries the date of its newest file; an archive with no other host, and
an archive root that cannot be resolved, each give the local counts with the
fleet named as not available and exit 0; a corrupt archived file is counted
as could not look, not as an empty session; `--local` reads no archive.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] A default run on a host whose archive holds other hosts counts their
  sessions per host and per runtime from the archive, and names each host
  with the date of its newest archived file
- [ ] The script opens no ssh connection: `FLEET_HOSTS`, the remote run and
  its flags are gone, with their tests and every statement of them
- [ ] An absent, unreadable or unresolvable archive, and an archive with no
  other host, are reported as such, with a non-zero exit only when no corpus
  at all is readable
- [ ] No decompressed transcript is written to disk
- [ ] `make check` passes
